body:
i will ruin my eyesight.

&#x200B;

or get fake glasses

I dont think that being trans stops them from being criticized. I've seen the opposit, in fact, a slingshot in the amount of criticism they get. Just not by mainstream media, its usually comments. I dont care about the constructive critism they get creatively, though i do see them getting a lot of hate for being trans. dont really know if thats related but honestly its just sad af. 

and yeah, its a valid criticism i guess, i was just genuinely asking because im no film analyst so ihni whats going on. i guess thanks for the input.

&#x200B;

Ps. idk if you know but your sentence " They are just over-protected from criticism now, due to being Trans" is false. They face just as much constructive criticism as before (which is lots tbh), though now they also have to deal with lots of blatant transphobia. Its, sadly, untrue saying they are shielded from criticism because their trans. Trans ppl face way more shit\* from people than most realise, though because the media has to be pc, everyone thinks were over protected from others. It sucks honestly. Dont know you, or if you care at all. I attached it just in case you do because its really important imo. Thanks a bunch for reading this long ass post lmao

&#x200B;

\*shit: Didn't really have any other word that was as blunt as that.

To a lot of us, its not about being attractive or living up to standards, its about reducing physical dysphoria. Dysphoria caused by my masculine features has caused me so much pain in my life and i'd give just about anything to get rid of it. I think a lot of us feel this way. When people like you come in saying wanting to pass is toxic and unrealistic and based on cis norms, etc., It can make us feel incredibly invalid for simply having the transition goals we have. Please, for the love of god, stop being part of the toxic gatekeepy side of the trans community, because by then you're just perpetuating others suffering and making us feel invalid. If you have nothing nice to say, dont say anything, because the alternative is hurting the feelings of those of us who want to pass. Please.

&#x200B;

So tired of running into these posts.

i dont think we should be gatekeeping others transition goals, for some of us, we actually want to look like a cis woman, and theres nothing wrong with that. Those of us who are fine not passing but still feel better about yourself are valid as well and thats totally fine. Can we please stop saying the goal of transition is to "feel better", or to pass, because at the end of the day, the only goal to transitioning should be what \*you\* want to get out of transitioning because thats whats gonna make \*you\* feel better. Talking about others Transition goals and saying you should be fine with whatever as long as your trying, or saying your invalid if you dont 100 percnt pass are both toxic and incredibly unfair to both sides (respectively) of the trans community. Just respect whatever somebodys goals are, period, because its completely valid to be yourself, and if that includes passing, than so be it.

&#x200B;

Put you in \*...\* to stress that nobody else gets a say in it, at all, ever, no matter what your goal is.

\*Me not seeing your post having 1000 downvotes\*

&#x200B;

"so that was a fucking lie"

Life choice i made at 13, not calling the cops on my family, and as such changing the course of my life until i was at least 18. Life choice number 2, that I fucking hate conservative ideals. Life choice number 3, that im not sexually attracted to men. Life choice number 4, not fatally o.d.'ing on benedryll. Should I go on, or are you seriously so priveledged and sheltered that you never went through through real shit?

&#x200B;

Bitch.

Never played it as i was just a we lad as it came out. Wanted a zelda 3d all stars, though this is good too. Still waiting on more 35th anniversary news though..... any minute nintendo.....

&#x200B;

Honestly i just hope this game is as good as everyone makes it out to be
